\subsection{Example 7: introgression of three genes}

Three target genes are distributed over chromosomes 1, 5 and 7, each with
two flanking markers.  Four scenarios compare \cde{t}, \cde{tb},
\cde{tfb}, and a program that uses a larger BC1 population followed by
\cde{tb} in later generations.

% MABC example: ex07
<<ex07_01,eval=FALSE>>=
rng.init(seed=2107)
@
The three-gene comparison uses one seed and a common set of four result files.

<<ex07_02,eval=FALSE>>=
mab.compare(
    a.simulation.name="fm013g-01",
    a.simulation.run="x",
    a.repetitions=NREP,
    a.linkage.map="ex-mab3.map",
    a.target.loci=c("target1","target2","target3"),
    a.flanking.loci=c(
        "umc90","umc27",
        "umc111","bnl1407",
        "umc37","bnl1518"
    ),
    a.gen.type=c("f1","bc","bc","bc"),
    a.population.size=c(1,100,100,100),
    a.sel.strategy=c("n","t","t","t"),
    b.simulation.name="fm013g-02",
    b.sel.strategy=c("n","tb","tb","tb"),
    c.simulation.name="fm013g-03",
    c.sel.strategy=c("n","tfb","tfb","tfb"),
    d.simulation.name="fm013g-04",
    d.population.size=c(1,200,100,100),
    d.sel.strategy=c("n","tfb","tb","tb"),
    result.files=c(
        "fm013g-01.RData",
        "fm013g-02.RData",
        "fm013g-03.RData",
        "fm013g-04.RData"
    )
)
@
Scenario A introduces three targets with target-only selection.  The
inherited scenarios compare \cde{tb}, \cde{tfb}, and a design with a larger
BC1 population followed by less intensive selection in later generations.

<<ex07_03,eval=FALSE>>=
out <- mab.tabulate(
    simulation.names.runs=c(
        "fm013g-01","x",
        "fm013g-02","x",
        "fm013g-03","x",
        "fm013g-04","x"
    ),
    RPG.gw.Q10=TRUE,
    TargetAlleles=TRUE,
    LinkageDrag=TRUE,
    MarkerAnalyses=TRUE,
    result.files=c(
        "fm013g-01.RData",
        "fm013g-02.RData",
        "fm013g-03.RData",
        "fm013g-04.RData"
    )
)
print(out)
@
All four programs are summarized together for target-allele recovery, the
