\subsection{Example 10: selection for a low number of donor segments}

Strategy \cde{tfs} combines target selection, flanking-marker preselection,
and selection for a low number of donor chromosome segments.  The final
segment-selection step is treated as an HT assay.  The same six BC1 starting
plants are compared.

% MABC example: ex10
<<ex10_01,eval=FALSE>>=
rng.init(seed=2111)
@
The donor-segment example uses the shared setup, its own seed, and the same
six observed BC1 donor candidates.

<<ex10_02,eval=FALSE>>=
mab.compare(
    a.simulation.name="bc1i1tfs",
    a.simulation.run="x",
    a.repetitions=NREP,
    a.donor.parent="ex-mabi1.mda",
    a.recurrent.parent="ex-mabp2.mda",
    a.linkage.map="ex-mab1.map",
    a.target.loci="target",
    a.flanking.loci=c("umc90","umc27"),
    a.gen.type=c("bc","bc"),
    a.population.size=c(100,100),
    a.sel.strategy=c("tfs","tfs"),
    a.no.selected=c(1,1),
    b.simulation.name="bc1i2tfs",
    b.donor.parent="ex-mabi2.mda",
    c.simulation.name="bc1i3tfs",
    c.donor.parent="ex-mabi3.mda",
    d.simulation.name="bc1i4tfs",
    d.donor.parent="ex-mabi4.mda",
    e.simulation.name="bc1i5tfs",
    e.donor.parent="ex-mabi5.mda",
    f.simulation.name="bc1i6tfs",
    f.donor.parent="ex-mabi6.mda",
    result.files=paste0("bc1i",1:6,"tfs.RData")
)
@
Strategy \cde{tfs} applies target and flanking-marker selection and then
favors plants with few donor chromosome segments.  The six inherited
scenarios differ only in which observed BC1 genotype starts the program.

<<ex10_03,eval=FALSE>>=
out <- mab.tabulate(
    simulation.names.runs=as.vector(rbind(
        paste0("bc1i",1:6,"tfs"),
        rep("x",6)
    )),
    RPG.gw.Q10=TRUE,
    DonorSegments.gw=TRUE,
    LinkageDrag=TRUE,
    result.files=paste0("bc1i",1:6,"tfs.RData")
)
print(out)
@
The resulting RPG, donor-segment, and linkage-drag summaries show how
explicit selection against donor segments can be used as an alternative
background criterion.

