\subsection{Example 13: success factor}

The \cde{success.factor} is the probability that a selected plant
contributes to the next generation, thereby representing survival and
fertility.  The example compares ten selected plants with success
probability 1, ten selected plants with probability 0.5, and five selected
plants with probability 1.

% MABC example: ex13
<<ex13_01,eval=FALSE>>=
rng.init(seed=2114)
@
The success-factor comparison is self-contained and fixes one common random seed.

<<ex13_02,eval=FALSE>>=
mab.compare(
    a.simulation.name="success-1",
    a.simulation.run="x",
    a.repetitions=NREP,
    a.linkage.map="ex-mab1.map",
    a.target.loci="target",
    a.flanking.loci=c("umc90","umc27"),
    a.gen.type=c("f1","bc","bc","bc","bc","bc"),
    a.population.size=c(1,100,100,100,100,100),
    a.sel.strategy=c("n","tb","tb","tb","tb","tb"),
    a.no.selected=c(1,10,10,10,10,10),
    a.success.factor=1,
    b.simulation.name="success-2",
    b.no.selected=c(1,10,10,10,10,10),
    b.success.factor=0.5,
    c.simulation.name="success-3",
    c.no.selected=c(1,5,5,5,5,5),
    c.success.factor=1,
    result.files=c(
        "success-1.RData",
        "success-2.RData",
        "success-3.RData"
    )
)
@
Scenario A selects ten plants per generation with success factor 1.
Scenario B gives each selected plant only 0.5 probability of contributing
to the next generation, while scenario C selects five plants with success
factor 1.

<<ex13_03,eval=FALSE>>=
out <- mab.tabulate(
    simulation.names.runs=c(
        "success-1","x",
        "success-2","x",
        "success-3","x"
    ),
    ext.summary=TRUE,
    RPG.gw.mean=TRUE,
    RPG.gw.Q10=TRUE,
    result.files=c(
        "success-1.RData",
        "success-2.RData",
        "success-3.RData"
    )
)
print(out)
@
The joint summary reports mean and lower-tail RPG.  This separates the
effect of biological success or fertility from the nominal number of plants
selected by the breeding program.

